<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices-March 6.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices-March 6.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for Mar 6</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Mar    200.50    205.00    207.50     219.00</p>
<p>    Apr    198.50    203.00    205.50     219.00</p>
<p>    May    198.50    203.00    205.50     219.00</p>
<p>    Jun    196.50    201.00    203.50     218.50</p>
<p>    Jul    195.00    199.50    202.50     217.00</p>
<p>    Aug    194.00    198.50    201.00     216.00</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$1.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	172.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  147.50	    Port Adelaide	 149.00</p>
<p>Gladstone     147.75	    Port Giles	    149.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	145.50	    Wallaroo		149.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    144.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     147.50	    Port Lincoln	  150.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   148.00	    Thevenard	     145.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 147.00	     Esperance	    152.25</p>
<p>    Portland	148.00	     Albany		 153.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    155.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    153.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid  </p>
<p>until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
